@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Plan
+
+## 1. Tests
+
+- [ ] 1.1 An assignment whose right side is a call with a lone string argument breaks after `=` the same way whether the string carries an unnecessary escape or not (tests/format/js/strings/escaped.js) [AC-1]
+- [ ] 1.2 The escaped and unescaped inputs print identically and stay stable when formatted again, for trailingComma all and es5 (tests/format/js/strings/__snapshots__/jsfmt.spec.js.snap) [AC-2]
+
+## 2. Fix
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Measure a lone string argument by its printed form when the assignment layout asks for it (src/language-js/utils/index.js, src/language-js/print/assignment.js)
+- [ ] 2.2 Changelog entry (changelog_unreleased/javascript/15525.md)
